    "texto2C2V_en": "9.1. <u>Indemnification by the Seller</u>. The Seller undertakes to defend, indemnify and hold harmless the Buyer, any of its Affiliates or any of their partners, officers, representatives, successors or assigns (or the partners, officers, representatives, successors or assigns of any of their Affiliates) and the Company (after the Closing Date) (&quot;<u>Buyer Indemnified Parties</u>&quot;), from and against any Losses suffered or incurred by a Buyer Indemnified Party that result, directly or indirectly, from any of the following events and circumstances:\n(a) any falsity, insufficiency, omission, error or inaccuracy in any representation or warranty made by the Seller pursuant to CLAUSE VIII and its Subclauses (and/or in any other document or instrument related to this Agreement); and/or\n(b) any and all acts or omissions, facts or omissions related to the Company, its Business or activities, of any nature, including, without limitation, labor, social security, tax, civil, insurance, financial, environmental or any other nature, in each case whose triggering event is related, directly and/or indirectly, in whole or in part, to the period prior to the Closing Date (inclusive), even if their effects only materialize in the future; and/or\n(c) non-compliance, partial or total, with any obligation of the Seller and/or the Company contained in this Agreement or in any document or instrument related to this Agreement; and/or\n(d) any and all active insufficiencies or passive contingencies with respect to the Base Financial Statements; and/or\n(e) acts, facts or omissions related to, or the responsibility of, the Seller or its respective Related Parties (except for the Company), occurring at any time, before or after the Closing Date, that are charged directly against the Buyer Indemnified Parties, including by reason of succession of the Seller, its Related Parties or Third Parties, piercing of the corporate veil or by reason of allegations of economic group characterization; and/or\n(f) eviction or any other defect or encumbrance that may affect the validity and/or effectiveness of the transactions through which the Buyer acquires the Acquired Shares, that prevents, hinders or threatens the ownership, possession and the free and unrestricted use, enjoyment and disposal, directly or indirectly, of the Acquired Shares by the Buyer.\n9.1.1. Even if the Buyer approves, or causes the approval of, the accounts and financial statements of any subsequent fiscal year of the Company, such approval shall not mean that the Buyer has waived its right to claim indemnification under this Clause 9.1, and the Seller shall remain bound as provided in this Agreement.\n9.1.2. The Seller's indemnification obligations established by this Agreement shall not be reduced or limited by (i) any audit or investigation conducted by the Buyer at the Company, before or after the execution of this Agreement; (ii) any exceptions to the representations and warranties made by the Seller, even if contained in the Schedules to which the respective clauses refer; (iii) any approval of the accounts of the officers or the financial statements of the Company after the Closing Date; (iv) any change, from the Closing Date onwards, in the practices adopted by the Company until the Closing Date, including tax, labor or accounting practices; and (v) any total or partial waiver by the Buyer of compliance with one or more Conditions Precedent.\n9.1.3. The Parties hereby agree that, in the event of indemnification in favor of a Buyer Indemnified Party, the Buyer may, at its sole discretion, choose which Buyer Indemnified Party shall be indemnified by the Seller, regardless of who suffered the Loss. The Buyer Indemnified Party chosen by the Buyer to be indemnified by the Seller must be communicated to the Seller together with the notice regarding the Loss, failing which the payment shall necessarily be made to the respective Buyer Indemnified Party that suffered the Loss. In the event of Losses suffered by the Company, if the Buyer determines that payment shall be made (i) directly to the Company, the indemnifiable amount shall correspond to 100% of the assessed Loss; or (ii) directly to the Buyer, the indemnifiable amount shall correspond to the percentage that the Acquired Shares represented in the Company's share capital on the Closing Date, applied to the total amount of the assessed Loss.\n9.1.4. Any Buyer Indemnified Party may, upon simple notice to the Seller, assign, at its sole discretion, its indemnification rights under this Clause to any Affiliate, without the need for consent or authorization. The Seller also agrees that, if the Buyer transfers, in whole or in part, its interest in the Company's share capital to any Third Party, the Buyer may assign, at its sole discretion, its indemnification rights under this Agreement in full or proportionally to the transferred interest, upon notice to the Seller, in which case the Third Party acquirer of the Buyer's interest in the Company's share capital shall have the right to receive, and the Seller shall be obligated to pay, the same indemnification assured to the Buyer Indemnified Parties under this Agreement.",
