    "texto2C2V_en": "6.1. <u>Conduct of Business</u>. Until the Closing Date, the Seller shall cause the Company's activities to be conducted in the Ordinary Course of Business, in a manner consistent with past practices (provided that such practices are in compliance with applicable Law), including with respect to the Company's operating costs. The Seller undertakes not to take, and not to permit the Company to take, without the prior consent of the Buyer, any of the following actions:\n(a) amend the Company's articles of association/bylaws;\n(b) transfer or create any Encumbrances on Shares issued by the Company, or assign or grant economic or voting rights attached to Shares issued by the Company;\n(c) approve the issuance of Shares or other securities of any kind or class, including subscription warrants and debentures, whether convertible or not, or grant options to purchase Shares issued by the Company;\n(d) approve any change to the Company's share capital, including through increase or reduction, split or reverse split, repurchase, redemption or amortization;\n(e) approve any merger (including share merger), spin-off, asset contribution (drop down), transformation, liquidation, dissolution or any corporate reorganization involving the Company;\n(f) incorporate a company, acquire an equity interest, establishment or set of assets, or enter into or form a joint venture, consortium or strategic alliance, or enter into any investment agreement, shareholders' agreement, or any other agreement containing financial contribution commitments, or dispose of, modify or terminate any such investments or commitments;\n(g) establish, amend or terminate any bonus plan or program, stock option plan and/or any other equity-based compensation or long-term incentive plan (including phantom stock);\n(h) declare, distribute or pay dividends, bonuses, interest on net equity, in cash, assets or credits, or make any other payment or distribution to the Seller, other shareholders/quotaholders or Related Parties, including by reimbursement or withdrawal;\n(i) dispose of, lease or create Encumbrances on items comprising the Company's non-current assets (property, plant and equipment, investments or intangibles);\n(j) enter into any transaction, or execute or amend any agreement between the Seller or the Seller's Related Parties and the Company;\n(k) incur, as borrower or lender, Indebtedness of any nature, in an individual amount (per transaction) exceeding R$[AMOUNT];\n(l) assume obligations of any nature, or make investments or incur expenses in an amount that, individually (per transaction) or in the aggregate (more than one transaction), exceeds R$[AMOUNT];\n(m) approve or permit the Company to grant any guarantee on obligations of Third Parties;\n(n) implement or carry out any collective reduction of employees, or otherwise implement any retirement program, voluntary severance program or any other program or effort to terminate employment agreements;\n(o) hire or dismiss employees holding a Key Position or modify the conditions of the Company's employees, including salaries, bonuses, incentives, indirect benefits, except (i) in the Ordinary Course of Business, (ii) if required by a Governmental Authority or as a result of collective bargaining agreements or collective disputes, or (iii) in the event of termination for cause, as provided by Law, provided that the Buyer is previously informed;\n(p) grant or announce any compensation increase, or promise or enter into any agreement or contract regarding the compensation of the Company's employees that results in an increase in personnel expenses in excess of [PERCENTAGE]% relative to the Base Date, including as a result of collective bargaining agreements or collective disputes;\n(q) modify, make or revoke any tax regime election or accounting method that affects Taxes collected by the Company, or file any amendment to tax returns, or fail to pay any Tax on the basis of an administrative or judicial decision that has not become final and unappealable;\n(r) change any accounting method or practice adopted by the Company, except as required by Law;\n(s) modify or revalue, reverse provisions or make any other adjustment to the book value of the Company's assets or liabilities, except as required by applicable accounting standards (CPC/IFRS) and carried out in a manner consistent with the Company's historically adopted accounting practices;\n(t) change the Company's commercial and/or administrative practices, including the usual payment cycles (accounts payable) or collection cycles (accounts receivable) of the Company, including through discounts or early payments;\n(u) settle, novate, waive or forgive any debt owed by any Person to the Company;\n(v) initiate, settle or waive rights in any Claim to which the Company is a party, or enter into or amend the terms of any commitment;\n(w) enter into, amend or terminate (i) any Material Agreement; (ii) any consulting or advisory agreement of any nature (including financial and marketing); (iii) any legal transaction containing any exclusivity, non-competition, non-solicitation, right of first refusal, right of first offer, or most favored nation provisions; or (iv) any agreement involving the sharing of costs, revenues, structure or results;\n(x) make any contribution to any political party, political candidate or Governmental Authority official;\n(y) approve or permit the implementation of any measure related to a judicial or out-of-court reorganization petition, voluntary bankruptcy filing, dissolution or liquidation of the Company;\n(z) approve or permit any transaction outside the Ordinary Course of Business;\n(aa) take any action that may affect, delay, render unfeasible or prevent the performance of the obligations assumed under this Agreement and/or the satisfaction of any Conditions Precedent by the Long-Stop Date.",
