    "texto2C2V_en": "8.1.16. <u>Assets</u>. The Company is the lawful possessor, owner or, as the case may be, lessee, borrower or leaseholder of all assets used in and necessary for the conduct and development of its Business (\"<u>Assets</u>\"). All Assets and rights of the Company are recorded in the Base Financial Statements at their respective acquisition cost, less any depreciation, as permitted by the Law and the Accounting Practices. All Assets are in good operating condition (except for ordinary wear and tear) and are free and clear of any Encumbrances. The Assets are sufficient and adequate for the continuity of the Business immediately after the Closing Date, in the same scope, volume, quality, margin and conditions currently practiced, without the need to acquire additional assets, rights, systems, equipment or agreements. No Asset is held, controlled, licensed or made available by Sellers, Related Parties or Third Parties without a valid agreement with the Company.",
