    "texto1C1V_en": "8.1.26. <u>Real Estate</u>. Schedule 8.1.26 contains a complete list of all leases of real estate properties (\"<u>Properties</u>\") to which the Company is a party (as lessee, sublessee, sublessor or lessor) (collectively, \"Real Estate Leases\"). The Company does not use or occupy any Property other than those listed in Schedule 8.1.26. Each Real Estate Lease is a valid and binding obligation of the Company and of the respective counterparties, and is in full force and effect. Neither the Company nor the respective counterparties are in default, and the Company has not received any communication from the lessee or the lessor, under any of the Real Estate Leases, alleging a breach by the Company of its obligations under the Real Estate Leases, including rent due and unpaid. The Company is the sole possessor of the leased Properties and has not assigned, sublet, licensed, shared, transferred or granted possession to Third Parties. No Real Estate Lease contains any change of control clause, restriction on the transfer of equity interests in the Company, acceleration, penalty, loss of renewal right, purchase option, right of first refusal or restriction that may be triggered by the Transaction. The Company does not own any Property. All buildings and structures used by it are in good operating condition (considering the wear and tear arising from normal and ordinary use) and are sufficient and adequate for the purposes for which they are currently being used. None of the buildings and structures (or any equipment located therein), nor the operation and maintenance of such buildings, violates any obligation imposed by any agreement or legal provision, or affects any property held by Third Parties. There is no debt related to the Properties with respect to Urban Property Tax – IPTU, Rural Property Tax – ITR, Real Estate Transfer Tax – ITBI, ground rents and/or laudêmios, or to the applicable condominium obligations and expenses. All Properties used by the Company are duly regularized in accordance with the Law, including, as applicable, with respect to operating permits, land use and occupancy licenses, AVCB (fire department certificate), habite-se (occupancy permit), sanitary and environmental licenses, accessibility, municipal registrations, condominium authorizations and other necessary approvals. The Company has not waived, taken or failed to take any action that it should have taken prior to the date of this Agreement that could nullify or cancel the full right to exercise any option, right of first offer or right of first refusal contained in any lease or sublease, including any option relating to purchase, renewal, extension or expiration contained in the Real Estate Leases.",
