    "texto1C1V_en": "8.1.28. <u>Customer and Supplier Portfolio; Consumer Protection</u>. Schedule 8.1.28 contains a list of (i) the main customers of the Company, considered as those that, in any of the last [TERM], have individually represented gross revenues exceeding R$[AMOUNT]; and (ii) the main suppliers of the Company, considered as those to which, in any of the last [TERM], the Company has paid amounts equal to or greater than R$[AMOUNT] (\"<u>Main Customers and Suppliers</u>\"). The Company has dealt with its customers and suppliers on a regular basis, and the consummation of the Transaction shall not prevent or jeopardize, in accordance with the agreements and understandings maintained between the Company and its customers and suppliers, the maintenance of the regular customer portfolio of the Company, the continuity of the provision of services to such customers and the regular supply by such suppliers. The Company adequately complies with all requirements of the Consumer Protection Law with respect to its relationships with suppliers and consumers, as well as its relationships with competitors. The Company has not received any notice from customers or suppliers regarding the breach of any contractual obligation, nor is it aware of any fact, act or event that could negatively impact the relationship of the Company with such customers and suppliers. The amounts owed to the suppliers of the Company are recorded in their entirety, and there are no extensions, arrangements, swaps or alternative payment methods involving any of such suppliers the recording of which is required by the Accounting Practices and which are not recorded in accordance with the Accounting Practices in the respective applicable financial statements. Since the Base Date, there have been no material extensions, arrangements, swaps or alternative payment methods involving any of such suppliers. Since the Base Date, none of the Main Customers and Suppliers has notified, informed, threatened or indicated an intention to terminate, reduce, suspend, change, renegotiate, not renew or adversely modify any commercial relationship with the Company, including as a result of the Transaction. There is no dependence on any customer, supplier, distributor, partner, representative, marketplace, platform, technology, raw material, input or sales channel not expressly disclosed in Schedule 8.1.28. All discounts, rebates, credits, allowances, bonuses, returns, penalties, SLAs, chargebacks, warranties and commercial obligations assumed before customers and suppliers are fully recorded and provisioned in accordance with the Accounting Practices.",
    "texto1C2V_en": "8.1.28. <u>Customer and Supplier Portfolio; Consumer Protection</u>. Schedule 8.1.28 contains a list of (i) the main customers of the Company, considered as those that, in any of the last [TERM], have individually represented gross revenues exceeding R$[AMOUNT]; and (ii) the main suppliers of the Company, considered as those to which, in any of the last [TERM], the Company has paid amounts equal to or greater than R$[AMOUNT] (\"<u>Main Customers and Suppliers</u>\"). The Company has dealt with its customers and suppliers on a regular basis, and the consummation of the Transaction shall not prevent or jeopardize, in accordance with the agreements and understandings maintained between the Company and its customers and suppliers, the maintenance of the regular customer portfolio of the Company, the continuity of the provision of services to such customers and the regular supply by such suppliers. The Company adequately complies with all requirements of the Consumer Protection Law with respect to its relationships with suppliers and consumers, as well as its relationships with competitors. The Company has not received any notice from customers or suppliers regarding the breach of any contractual obligation, nor is it aware of any fact, act or event that could negatively impact the relationship of the Company with such customers and suppliers. The amounts owed to the suppliers of the Company are recorded in their entirety, and there are no extensions, arrangements, swaps or alternative payment methods involving any of such suppliers the recording of which is required by the Accounting Practices and which are not recorded in accordance with the Accounting Practices in the respective applicable financial statements. Since the Base Date, there have been no material extensions, arrangements, swaps or alternative payment methods involving any of such suppliers. Since the Base Date, none of the Main Customers and Suppliers has notified, informed, threatened or indicated an intention to terminate, reduce, suspend, change, renegotiate, not renew or adversely modify any commercial relationship with the Company, including as a result of the Transaction. There is no dependence on any customer, supplier, distributor, partner, representative, marketplace, platform, technology, raw material, input or sales channel not expressly disclosed in Schedule 8.1.28. All discounts, rebates, credits, allowances, bonuses, returns, penalties, SLAs, chargebacks, warranties and commercial obligations assumed before customers and suppliers are fully recorded and provisioned in accordance with the Accounting Practices.",
