    "texto2C2V_en": "8.1.35. <u>Good Practices</u>. The Company has an integrity program in force, which includes an outsourced whistleblower channel, and there have been no reports in the last [TERM]. The Company, including through any employee, officer, manager, agent, consultant or any other Person, (i) has not violated and does not violate any Laws applicable to money laundering or currency evasion; (ii) has not violated and does not violate any Anti-Corruption Laws; (iii) has not offered, paid, committed to pay, promised to pay or authorized the payment of money or other things of value, contribution, expense reimbursement, gifts, benefits or delivered any kind of property to any person who is an officer, agent, employee or representative of any Governmental Authority, or to any existing or potential customer (whether or not related to a Governmental Authority), or to any political party, any candidate for public office or political party offices, or to any other Person, knowing or having reason to believe that all or any part of the money or thing of value offered, given or promised would facilitate or seek to facilitate (a) obtaining favorable treatment in the Business, (b) would reward favorable treatment in the Business, (c) would facilitate or seek to facilitate obtaining special concessions or would serve as payment for special concessions already obtained, in favor of, or in relation to, the Sellers or the Company, or (d) would constitute a violation of Anti-Corruption Laws. The Company has adequate practices and policies to prevent non-compliance with Anti-Corruption Laws by its employees, officers, managers, agents, consultants or any other Person related to the Company. The Company, its shareholders and/or their respective Related Parties have not made any self-disclosure or entered into any collaboration or leniency agreements with Governmental Authorities. Neither the Sellers nor the Company provide services to Governmental Authorities.",
